{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using SwiftData?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration"},{"type":"text","text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project","level":2,"anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Ensembles package to your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles-3.git"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"]},{"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit","level":2,"anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer"},{"type":"text","text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically."}]},{"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model","level":3,"anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode, add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".xcdatamodeld"},{"type":"text","text":" file to your project (e.g., "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Model.xcdatamodeld"}]},{"type":"text","text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Note"},{"type":"text","text":" entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueID"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) attributes."}]},{"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`","level":3,"anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For deduplication, conform your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"type":"text","text":" subclass to the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"]},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A global identifier "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"must never change","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object."}]},{"text":"3. Set Up the Container","level":3,"anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewContext"},{"text":" so your UI stays up to date.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional","type":"heading","text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location","type":"heading","text":"Using a Custom Store Location","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeURL"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"]},{"anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack","type":"heading","text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you already have an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentContainer"},{"text":", pass it in directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Or if you have an existing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObjectContext"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration","type":"heading","text":"Auto-Sync Configuration","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control when syncing occurs with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"autoSyncPolicy"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".manual"},{"text":" and call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()"},{"text":" yourself for full control over timing.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2","type":"heading","text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to ","type":"text"},{"code":".ensembles3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble","type":"heading","text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Create-and-Attach","type":"heading","text":"Create and Attach","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier"},{"text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry.","type":"text"}]}]},{"anchor":"Sync-Changes","type":"heading","text":"Sync Changes","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate","text":"Handle the Delegate","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"},{"type":"text","text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"text":" subclasses conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},{"text":", you don’t need to implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects"},{"text":" — the ensemble discovers identifier properties automatically. You only need the delegate method if you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly without ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"tip","type":"aside","name":"Tip"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other delegate methods let you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inspect and repair merge data"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" before it’s committed (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handle save failures","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" during merging ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"React to forced detaches"}]},{"text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption (","type":"text"},{"code":"didDetachWithError:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Detach","text":"Detach","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:"}]},{"code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing."}]},{"anchor":"Seed-Policies","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Seed Policies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy"},{"text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData"},{"text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData"},{"type":"text","text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Sync-Options","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Options"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For advanced control, pass ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Process Pending Changes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()"},{"text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChanges()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Monitor-Activity","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Monitor Activity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Track long-running operations via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress"},{"text":", or observe these notifications:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidBeginActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — An activity started"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidMakeProgressWithActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — Progress updated (includes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AttachingPhase"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — An activity finished (may include an error)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncingPhase":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The phase of a sync operation currently in progress."}],"title":"SyncingPhase","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyncingPhase"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncingphase","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyncingPhase"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsembleContainer/sync()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach if needed and merge changes with peers."}],"title":"sync()","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemblecontainer\/sync()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sync"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/Syncable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A protocol for model types that declare how to derive a global identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Ensembles deduplication."}],"title":"Syncable","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Syncable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncable","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Syncable"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncOptions":{"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncoptions","title":"SyncOptions","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SyncOptions","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Options that control which phases of a sync are executed."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyncOptions"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Ensembles","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy/excludeLocalData":{"title":"SeedPolicy.excludeLocalData","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Do not import local data. You will usually want to delete the store before attaching."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/seedpolicy\/excludelocaldata","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"excludeLocalData"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy/mergeAllData":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Import the local store contents and merge them with cloud data at the next merge."}],"title":"SeedPolicy.mergeAllData","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/seedpolicy\/mergealldata","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeAllData"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsembleContainer":{"kind":"symbol","title":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemblecontainer","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A high-level container that sets up a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with automatic syncing,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"delegate management, and optional Core Data stack creation.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SwiftDataIntegration":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","title":"SwiftData Integration","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync SwiftData models with Ensembles using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDataEnsembleContainer"},{"type":"text"